{"availability":"available","full":"m2c2-project/m2c2kit","name":"m2c2kit","description":"m2c2kit is a library for cross-platform cognitive assessments","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":26,"forks":7,"created":"2022-01-10T20:19:21Z","updated":"2026-09-04T05:21:08Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://m2c2-project.github.io/m2c2kit-docs/","topics":[],"demo":"https://m2c2-project.github.io/m2c2kit-docs/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:34:00.423Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:34:00.423Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:34:00.423Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.356Z","stars":26,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-12T13:34:00.423Z","stars":26,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["an open-source library for cross-platform cognitive assessments","m2c2kit is a library for cross-platform cognitive assessments. It is produced by the Ambulatory Methods for Measuring Cognitive Change research project (Award #U2CAG060408), sponsored by the National Institute on Aging.","m2c2kit is written in Typescript and leverages Google's canvaskit-wasm Skia-based graphics engine to present cognitive assessments using HTML5 and JavaScript."],"features":["Mobile first. Optimized for touch and mobile devices while also usable on desktops.","Portable. Use on browsers, compile within native apps using webviews, or embed in products like Qualtrics. A shared assessment codebase reduces development time and promotes experiment standardization across devices and…","Rapid iteration. Quickly develop and test new assessments with the JavaScript-based library and deploy them in studies."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/m2c2-project/m2c2kit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"13dfbcb25793e893e47601a6c090f412519101b51ddeb8307090a3af1ec227c3","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.461Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.461Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"an open-sour